  "description_html": "Restoration of a juvenile <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tarbosaurus\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tarbosaurus\">Tarbosaurus</a> bataar</i>. The illustration is based on a juvenile <i>Tarbosaurus</i> which died about 3 years old,.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and measured about 2.1 meters (about 7 feet) long (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://scienceblogs.com/laelaps/2008/07/a_new_juvenile_tarbosaurus.php\">see it on <i>Scienceblogs</i></a>, []<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/25829787/\" href=\"https://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/25829787/\"><i>msnbc</i></a> and <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://search.japantimes.co.jp/cgi-bin/nn20080725a4.html\"><i>japantimes</i></a> for sources). The feathers are a guess, based on the idea that young tyrannosaurs had some kind of insulating feathers.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Tsuihiji T <i>et.al.</i> (2011), <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.oucom.ohiou.edu/dbms-witmer/Downloads/2011_Tsuihiji_et_al._Tarbosaurus_juvenile_skull.pdf\">\"Cranial Osteology of a Juvenile Specimen of <i>Tarbosaurus bataar</i> (Theropoda, Tyrannosauridae) from the Nemegt Formation (Upper Cretaceous) of Bugin Tsav, Mongolia\"</a>, <i>Journal of Vertebrate Paleontology</i> <b>31</b>(3): p. 497-517.</span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
